{
 "_about": "One row per clip to fetch from Mixamo on the BOG (tools/mixamo_fetch.py). `file` is the FBX name that lands in anims/, `role` is the game's name for the move; one row per role (D-096 chose each from the candidates fetched and deleted the rest). A row with `mixamo_query` instead of `mixamo_id` fetches every search result as `<file>-<Name>`, or only those named in `mixamo_keep`. `in_place` is false everywhere on purpose: Mixamo's in-place export flattens the hip bob along with the travel, so travel is stripped at import instead, where it also yields the authored speed. `loop` is provisional until the animator is rebuilt. `face` is how the import turns the clip onto the body's forward: `hips` squares the hip line to the rest pose, `chest` squares the shoulder line (the strafes, D-066), `none` trusts Mixamo's world frame (the archer set aims down it; a slide and a dive travel down it). `markers` are the clip's events in seconds, written onto the Animation as markers for the animator to read (D-097).",
 "fps": 30,
